{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf93rTd9VudkwpmCqqXMP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! All tests pass. Let me verify the implementation covers all requirements by reviewing the key changes:\n\n1. **Partial fulfilment** ✅\n   - Order and Shipment models now have `quantity` field\n   - Shipment status enum includes `DELIVERED`\n   - Order tracks fulfilment with allocated, delivered, and status\n   - Shipment allocation validation prevents exceeding order quantity\n   - Shipment transitions: `/confirm`, `/deliver`, `/cancel`\n   - `GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS` filters by status\n   - `PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity` updates order quantity with validation\n   - Cancelled shipments release their quantity\n\n2. **Customer validation** ✅\n   - `POST /orders` rejects orders for non-existent customers with HTTP 422\n   - `GET /customers/{customerId}` returns 404 with error envelope\n   - Updated `OrderControllerTest` to create customers before orders\n\n3. **Paged lists** ✅\n   - All list endpoints (`GET /customers`, `/orders`, `/shipments`) accept `limit` and `offset`\n   - Pagination parameters validated (limit 1-100, offset >= 0)\n   - `X-Total-Count` header returned with total count before slicing\n   - Results sorted by ID\n\nLet me create a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary of Implementation\n\nI've successfully implemented all three features requested in BE-005:\n\n### 1. Partial Fulfilment\n- Added `quantity` field to Order and Shipment models (default 1, min 1)\n- Added `DELIVERED` status to ShipmentStatus enum\n- Implemented fulfilment tracking: allocated (sum of non-cancelled shipments), delivered (sum of delivered shipments)\n- Added order fulfilment status calculation: UNALLOCATED → PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED → FULLY_ALLOCATED → DELIVERED\n- Implemented shipment allocation validation (HTTP 409 when exceeding order quantity)\n- Added shipment state transitions:\n  - `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`: CREATED → CONFIRMED\n  - `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver`: CONFIRMED → DELIVERED\n  - `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel`: CREATED → CANCELLED\n- Added quantity amendment: `PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity` with validation\n\n### 2. Customer Validation\n- Orders now require existing customer (HTTP 422 for unknown customer)\n- Customer 404 responses now use error envelope with CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND code\n- Updated OrderControllerTest to create customers before creating orders\n\n### 3. Paged Lists\n- Added pagination support to all list endpoints with `limit` (1-100, default 100) and `offset` (default 0)\n- Implemented `X-Total-Count` header with count after filtering (for orders with fulfilment filter)\n- Added input validation for pagination parameters (HTTP 400 for invalid values)\n- Maintains unpaged behavior for calls without parameters\n\n### Code Quality\n- No new Maven dependencies added\n- All existing tests pass\n- Consistent error handling using the API error envelope\n- Kotlin Spring Boot architecture preserved\n\nThe build passes with 13 tests all passing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":918,"cache_read_input_tokens":66209,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":918},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2cc719a-1041-4c33-a199-5ee2b9efe400","uuid":"55cef52d-e90f-466f-9ee3-2450b38dec60","timestamp":"2026-09-17T12:57:44.179Z","request_id":"req_011Cf93rTBMMZNy7ECsj94Fs"}
